// probity.config.ts — TEMPLATE (controlled-build-run-kit).
//
// Probity is the TDD + naming guard. The PreToolUse hook runs
// `node_modules/.bin/probity --agent claude-code (npx @1.8.1 fallback)` before every Write/Edit/Bash;
// THIS file tells it which files to guard and what to forbid. It is the single
// most repo-specific file in the kit — adapt every glob to YOUR source tree.
//
// Docs: https://www.npmjs.com/package/@nizos/probity
//
// PORTING CHECKLIST:
//   1. Set the `files` globs to your production code (the reference host used 'packages/**/*.py').
//   2. Keep enforceTdd() — it is the whole point (no prod code before a watched-fail test).
//   3. Replace/remove the naming bans below with YOUR repo's rules (or delete them).
//   4. See examples/reference-probity.config.ts for the real, worked reference version.

